        <div><a name="_slavic" id="_slavic"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.40 Slavic</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_282956e2-0099-4f93-aa89-ea497139dd49" id="_282956e2-0099-4f93-aa89-ea497139dd49"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo37;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo37;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo37;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    patronymic name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3a828848-dae6-4d42-bcb1-ad597903541b" id="_3a828848-dae6-4d42-bcb1-ad597903541b"></a>Slavic naming applies to Russian, Ukrainian, Belorussian,
Bulgaria, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Serbia and Macedonia,
as well as some populations of Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan and Turkmenistan.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_13" id="_typical_name_patterns_13"></a><p class="h3Annex">B.40.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.47</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_f1f9a159-6e7e-4149-95f3-0ba44da1276a" id="_f1f9a159-6e7e-4149-95f3-0ba44da1276a"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">patronymic name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples_13" id="_examples_13"></a><p class="h3Annex">B.40.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_a5f8aa83-f797-43c5-b9c9-1b0836ee3bea" id="_a5f8aa83-f797-43c5-b9c9-1b0836ee3bea"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x418;&#x432;&#x430;&#x301;&#x43D; &#x41A;&#x43E;&#x43D;&#x441;&#x442;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x442;&#x438;&#x301;&#x43D;&#x43E;&#x432;&#x438;&#x447; &#x410;&#x439;&#x432;&#x430;&#x437;&#x43E;&#x301;&#x432;&#x441;&#x43A;&#x438;&#x439; (&#x201C;Ivan Konstantinovich Aivazovsky&#x201D;). Ivan is the given name, Konstantinovich the patronymic name, Aivazovsky the family name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_a596afdd-ec6e-4413-9f77-bfe8120deb1d" id="_a596afdd-ec6e-4413-9f77-bfe8120deb1d"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x41E;&#x43B;&#x435;&#x43A;&#x441;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x434;&#x440; &#x406;&#x432;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x43E;&#x432;&#x438;&#x447; &#x411;&#x456;&#x43B;&#x430;&#x448;, (&#x201C;Oleksandr Ivanovych Bilash&#x201D;).  Oleksandr is the given name, Ivanovych the patronymic name, Bilash the family name.</p></div></div></div>
